## Content Pipeline (fetch_news.py)

```
Fetch (3 API providers + 19 RSS) → Normalize → Dedup (3-layer) → Bundle (≤50/doc) → upload_bundles() → article_bundles
```

Short field names in each bundle: `i`=id, `t`=title, `d`=description, `img`=imageUrl, `u`=articleUrl, `p`=publishedAt (ms), `s`=sourceName, `c`=category, `tr`=trending (1 if trending, omitted otherwise)

### Deduplication Layers
1. **Article ID hash** — SHA-256 of (normalize_title(title) + normalized_source)
2. **URL dedup** — seen_urls set within RSS processing
3. **Cross-run cache** — `.article_cache.json` persisted via actions/cache

### URL-Based Category Override
After fetching from RSS, `url_derived_category(article_url, feed_category)` checks the article URL path against `URL_CATEGORY_SIGNALS` (defined after `RSS_FEEDS`). First match wins and overrides the feed-assigned category. Fixes RSS feeds that leak articles from other sections (e.g. abplive.com/education/feed publishing entertainment articles). Logs `[cat-fix]` to stdout when an override fires.

### Provider Tagging
Every article gets `_provider` key (`currentsapi` / `rss` / `newsdata` / `contextualweb`).
Stripped before Firebase upload (short field mapping in `upload_bundles`).

### Category Short Codes (CATEGORY_SHORT dict)
API source categories normalized then mapped: pol/cri/int/def→nat, stk→bus, sci→tec. Short codes: `nat`, `bus`, `spt`, `ent`, `tec`, `hlt`, `edu`.
RSS feeds use short codes directly in their `category` field.

### Quality Gate
MIN_TITLE_LEN=15, MIN_DESC_LEN=100; spt/ent/nat can pass with MIN_DESC_TRENDING=30.

### Trending (plan 26)
24h filter, cluster by normalize_title, freq≥2 distinct sources. Add `tr`:1 for trending articles only.

